From 60d7a38333c9d1afda20dfae53fb370d28b4ab26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:48:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/37] nas-relay: run natively on DSM with a usbfs backend;
 tested on real hardware

The DS416j (ARMv7, DSM 7.4.1) has no Container Manager and no libusb-1.0,
so the relay now also talks to the QMX through Linux usbfs directly
(ctypes ioctl: iso/bulk URBs, control, set-interface, claim/release),
picking libusb when it loads and usbfs otherwise (QMX_BACKEND overrides).

- start-relay.sh / stop-relay.sh / env.sh: native install, started at
  boot by a root Task Scheduler task; supervisor restarts the relay
- --selftest / --selftest-only: read-only check of I/Q, CAT and ports 2/3
- nettest.py + check.sh: network test against the running relay
- get_libusb1.py: optional python-libusb1 fetch, SHA-256 pinned
- README: DSM native install first, Docker kept for other models
- PDF regenerated with the native install and hardware results

Tested on a Synology DS416j with a QMX+: self-test passed (47,993 I/Q
pairs/s, CAT ID/FA/MD/VN, 3 serial ports) and the network test passed
(47,680 pairs/s over TCP, CAT, Radio menus port, PC on 7356 alongside
the Tab5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
